DTSTAMP:20260505T111800Z
UID:event-assignment-1604886
DTSTART:20260527T045900Z
DTEND:20260527T045900Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:----------------------------------------\nModule 1Paediatric Or
 thopaedic Case Quiz\n----------------------------------------\n\n  Instru
 ctions\n--------------\n\nYou can find the case “Paediatric Orthopaedic 
 Clinic at the Children's Hospital of Western Ontario” in the readings pa
 cket\, the link for which is available in the syllabus.\n\nThis quiz does 
 not assume knowledge of process analysis concepts (Module 2). This quiz co
 nsists of ten true/false statements\, set to appear in random order\, abou
 t facts in the case that are relevant for analyzing the case and will be h
 elpful when we discuss the case in the live session\, followed by one shor
 t-essay question (50 to 100 words for response) that requires you to repor
 t your instinctive solution and reasoning based on your reading of the cas
 e. For your response to the short-essay question\, please feel free to rel
 y on your work and/or consumer experience or your knowledge of related con
 cepts in addition to information from the case. As a reminder\, you are no
 t required to complete process analysis (Module 2) to respond to any of th
 e questions on this quiz. \n\nThis quiz is not timed and you are allowed 
 three attempts before the deadline\, the latest attempt before the deadlin
 e will be graded. You are allowed these three attempts in case you change 
 your mind about any response before the due date. Note that these attempts
  are not meant to enable you to see and improve your score - you will not 
 be able to immediately see what you submitted or your score. Also note tha
 t any time you reopen a quiz in Canvas after submitting\, Canvas creates a
  fresh submission and you are not able to see and use your responses from 
 the previous submission. So\, in case you decide to resubmit\, you will ne
 ed to respond to all the questions.\n\nIt is always a good idea to note yo
 ur responses when submitting a quiz. You will only be able to see your sub
 mitted responses\, your score\, and the correct answers on Canvas after we
  have completed grading of the quiz for all the learners.\n\nAcademic inte
 grity and honesty are essential and non-negotiable at the University of Il
 linois. It is your duty to not only understand and abide by University gui
 delines (read Article I\, Part 4: Academic Integrity of the Illinois Stude
 nt Code)\, but also to promote a culture of ethical behavior within your g
 roup and class. Ignorance is not an excuse for any academic dishonesty. Vi
 olations will be handled via Department\, School\, and University policies
 .
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Case Quiz: Paediatric Orthopaedic [badm_567_120265_260488]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://canvas.illinois.edu/calendar?include_contexts=course_
 69166&month=05&year=2026#assignment_1604886
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://instructu
 re-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_145590000000000001/attachments/2176028
 9/mobile_app.css"><div id="dp-wrapper" class="dp-wrapper dp-flat-sections 
 variation-2"><header class="dp-header dp-flat-sections variation-2 " style
 ="margin-bottom: 0px\; padding-bottom: 15px\; padding-top: 40px\;">\n<h2 c
 lass="dp-heading"><span class="dp-header-pre">Module 1</span><span class="
 dp-header-title">Paediatric Orthopaedic Case Quiz</span></h2>\n</header>\n
 <div class="dp-content-block kl_content_block_0">\n<h3 class="dp-has-icon"
 ><i class="fas fa-map" style="color: #ff5f05\;" aria-hidden="true"><span c
 lass="dp-icon-content" style="display: none\;">&nbsp\;</span></i> Instruct
 ions</h3>\n<p><span>You can find the case “Paediatric Orthopaedic Clinic
  at the Children's Hospital of Western Ontario” in the readings packet\,
  the link for which is available in the syllabus.</span></p>\n<p><span><st
 rong>This quiz does not assume knowledge of process analysis concepts (Mod
 ule 2). </strong>This quiz consists of <strong>ten true/false statements</
 strong>\,<strong> </strong>set to appear in random order\,<strong> </stron
 g>about facts in the case that are relevant for analyzing the case and wil
 l be helpful when we discuss the case in the live session\, followed by <s
 trong>one short-essay question</strong> (50 to 100 words for response) tha
 t requires you to report your instinctive solution and reasoning based on 
 your reading of the case. For your response to the short-essay question\, 
 please feel free to rely on your work and/or consumer experience or your k
 nowledge of related concepts in addition to information from the case. As 
 a reminder\, you are not required to complete process analysis (Module 2) 
 to respond to any of the questions on this quiz.&nbsp\;</span></p>\n<p><sp
 an>This quiz is not timed and you are allowed <strong>three</strong> attem
 pts before the deadline\, the latest attempt before the deadline will be g
 raded. You are allowed these three attempts in case you change your mind a
 bout any response before the due date. Note that these attempts are not me
 ant to enable you to see and improve your score - you will not be able to 
 immediately see what you submitted or your score. <strong>Also note that a
 ny time you reopen a quiz in Canvas after submitting\, Canvas creates a fr
 esh submission and you are not able to see and use your responses from the
  previous submission. So\, in case you decide to resubmit\, you will need 
 to respond to all the questions.</strong></span></p>\n<p><span><strong>It 
 is always a good idea to note your responses when submitting a quiz. You w
 ill only be able to see your submitted responses\, your score\, and the co
 rrect answers on Canvas after we have completed grading of the quiz for al
 l the learners.</strong></span></p>\n<p><span>Academic integrity and hones
 ty are essential and non-negotiable at the University of Illinois. It is y
